<%# One button, two states. Whichever is showing, the other is one click away.

    Pressing it swaps the heart where it stands, and moves nothing else. It used
    to be a full page visit: the scroll jumped back to the top of the record, the
    page faded in all over again, and the history filled with the same URL, once
    per heart. Somebody pressing a heart is telling you about a song, not asking
    to be taken somewhere.

    A record is hearted with the same heart as a song, because it is the same
    gesture. It only sits bigger, in the header where a record's own buttons are —
    and the size travels with the press, so what comes back is the same heart. %>
<% liked = Current.profile.likes?(thing) %>
<% big = local_assigns.fetch(:size, "small").to_s == "large" %>
<span id="<%= dom_id(thing, :heart) %>" class="shrink-0">
  <%= button_to [ thing, :like ],
                method: liked ? :delete : :post,
                params: { size: big ? "large" : "small" },
                "aria-label": "#{liked ? "Unlike" : "Like"} #{thing.title}",
                class: "heart group/heart cursor-pointer rounded-full transition active:scale-90
                        #{big ? "p-3" : "p-2"}
                        #{liked ? "text-accent hover:text-accent-bright" : "text-neutral-500 hover:text-white"}" do %>
    <%# The heart it just became beats once. A control that gives nothing back
        when you press it is the cheapest juice in a music app, left on the floor. %>
    <svg class="<%= big ? "size-5" : "size-4" %> transition-transform group-hover/heart:scale-110 <%= "is-beating" if liked %>"
         viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="<%= liked ? "currentColor" : "none" %>"
         stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M8 14S1.5 9.7 1.5 5.6A3.6 3.6 0 0 1 8 3.5a3.6 3.6 0 0 1 6.5 2.1C14.5 9.7 8 14 8 14Z"/>
    </svg>
  <% end %>
</span>
